OpenNCALayer is an independent reimplementation of the NCALayer protocol and of the
operations behind it. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the National Certification
Authority of the Republic of Kazakhstan. "NCALayer" and "Kalkan" are used only to describe
compatibility.

The workspace builds oncl-gost and oncl-pki against locally modified copies of the
RustCrypto `streebog` 0.11.0 and `hmac` 0.13.0 crates (additive secret-input variants of
the key-agreement and key-wrap paths; the public-document hash and HMAC paths are unchanged).
Both are MIT OR Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) The RustCrypto Project Developers and Artyom
Pavlov. The modified sources and the full notice are in the repository's `vendor/` and
`NOTICE`; this package does not contain them.

`roots/` contains the public CA certificates of the National Certification Authority of the
Republic of Kazakhstan (production PKI), exactly as the original NCALayer ships them in
`cacerts.jks`. They are public documents distributed for free use; the rights to the
certificates belong to their issuer and are not licensed under Apache-2.0. Their SHA-256 sums
are in the source repository's `fixtures/nca/SHA256SUMS`, which this package does not contain.

`testing-data/rsa.pk8.der` is a synthetic RSA private key generated for tests. It protects
nothing and has no value; it is used only by the `testing` feature's mocks (a secret scanner
that flags this file is a false positive).
